 "_note": "LoG2 armour and fighter figures. Slots: BF animation slot -> LoG2 animation. LoG2's own numbering (Nov 10, read off the frames): 0 idle, 1 walk, 2 hurt (sweat marks), 3 hit and fall, 4 flinch, 5 ki (fist in, palm out, arm out), 6-8 melee, 9 changing into the next form (only the records that change), 11 power-up (fists in, then both arms up; front only), 12 flying, 13 dash (the run; only the player-style records), 16 charged hit, 18 the record's own firing pose where it has one (the armour records' 18 is a slash). build.py fills the slots that depend on what a record has: 2 run (13, or the walk), 13 power-up (11, or the idle), 15 flying (12), 10 the change (9 where the record has it; fighter_poses does the rest). Beams and balls held (18) show the arm out (ki frame 2); Kamehameha-code moves use slot 31 (fighter_poses: the fist in, then the arm out). extra_slots: 22 = the dash (LoG2 13) for the charged melee's run-in, 23 = charged hit (16); Vegeta's 24 = LoG2's ki charge, hands together (14) for the armour Vegetas' Galick Gun pose (build.py armour_pose). Teen Gohan (Nov 12): his purple gi is LoG2's r50 (long black hair); his Super Saiyan and 2 in it are r50's animations with the frames teen.py makes (log2_source: 'ss' or 'ss2', the owner's approved frames, Nov 11), for the animations teen.ANIMS has. The rest is what the armour Super Saiyan 2 figure does where LoG2 has no frames: no change of their own (10: fighter_poses, LOG2_CHANGES), Super Saiyan 2's power-up the stance (13) and its flying the hit (15); the charged hit (23) is their first combo hit (6), as base armour Gohan's. \"last\": built after every other actor (build.py add_actors), so adding one moves no id that scripts, rigs or saves know.",
